I need a review of the payment callback path in this Spring Boot service and a delivery plan with a rough estimate. The important question is not style: under provider retries, two application instances can both observe a missing `PaymentAttempt`, publish `PaymentCaptured`, and charge the order twice. Review the design across `PaymentWebhookController`, `PaymentAttemptService`, `OutboxPublisher`, and the database migration, then tell me what must change before we call it production-ready.

```java
@Transactional
public void accept(ProviderEvent event) {
  if (!attemptRepo.existsByProviderId(event.id())) {
    attemptRepo.save(PaymentAttempt.from(event));
    outbox.save(new OutboxMessage("PaymentCaptured", event.orderId()));
  }
}
```

