`firmware/src/TelemetryBuffer.cpp` currently contains:

```cpp
static volatile uint8_t head;
static volatile uint8_t tail;
static Sample slots[16];

void TelemetryBuffer::pushFromIsr(const Sample& s) {
    slots[head] = s;
    head = (head + 1) & 0x0f;
    if (head == tail) {
        tail = (tail + 1) & 0x0f;
        dropped++;
    }
}

bool TelemetryBuffer::pop(Sample& out) {
    __disable_irq();
    if (tail == head) {
        __enable_irq();
        return false;
    }
    out = slots[tail];
    tail = (tail + 1) & 0x0f;
    __enable_irq();
    return true;
}
```

`pushFromIsr()` is called by `drivers/adc_dma.cpp` at 8 kHz. The main loop drains it every 250 ms, then `FlashJournal::append()` writes a 32-byte record. The board has a single-core Cortex-M0+, and `Sample` is currently 12 bytes. There is a watchdog reset if the drain takes longer than 40 ms. The existing tests in `test/telemetry_buffer_test.cpp` run only on the host and do not model an interrupt arriving while `pop()` copies a slot.

